<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        Channels are created automatically: one for each active location, and one for the whole company. Who's in
        them follows where people work, so there's nothing to add by hand. On
        <a href="/manage/chat/channels">Chat Channels</a>, Managers see their own location's channel. Admins see
        every location's channel and the company channel.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="For each channel">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Open</strong>: go to the channel in Chat.</li>
            <li><strong>Staff can post</strong>: turn it off to make the channel announcement-only. Staff can still read it.</li>
            <li><strong>Write a pinned post</strong>: stays at the top of the channel until it's unpinned, and everyone in
                the channel is notified.</li>
        </ul>
        <FluentText>
            In the channel itself, managers can also pin or unpin any message, and <strong>Remove for everyone</strong>.
            <strong>Removed in the last 30 days</strong> lists what's been taken down and by whom.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
